    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nSet on an elevated site of approximately one acre, this impressive four-bedroom stone-fronted residence enjoys breathtaking panoramic views across the surrounding countryside, the Atlantic Ocean and towards the Aran Islands. The residence is approached by a pea-gravel driveway with a paddock extending from the front to the side and rear of the property. To the rear an extensive paved patio with attractive cut-stone walls extends the full length of the rear of the property.Internally, the accommodation is bright, spacious and well-proportioned throughout. The ground floor comprises of an entrance porch and hallway, a substantial open-plan kitchen/living/dining area with views of the Atlantic, a separate utility, games room, double bedroom and shower room. A bespoke wrought-iron staircase with polished timber steps leads to the first floor.The spacious first-floor landing provides an additional living area with floor-to-ceiling gable end windows with stunning uninterrupted views across the countryside to the Atlantic Ocean and Aran Islands. Three further generous double bedrooms, one with en-suite, together with a separate shower room complete the first-floor accommodation.The property benefits from oil-fired central heating, mains water and a septic tank.The property offers convenient access to Doolin, Lisdoonvarna, the Burren, the Cliffs of Moher and Lahinch. The wider area is renowned for its dramatic coastline, traditional music, golf courses, and a wide range of outdoor and coastal activities. With generous accommodation, an approximately one-acre site and exceptional Atlantic and Aran Island views, this distinctive property offers a wonderful opportunity as a permanent family home or impressive coastal retreat.Viewing is highly recommended and strictly by prior appointment with sole selling agents. PSL 002295"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Porch - 1.55m x 1.3m\nA lead glass teak front door gives access to the entrance porch with tile flooring and opens out into the main hallway.\n\nEntrance Hallway - 5.2m x 3.05m\nTile flooring, rear and front aspect windows, bespoke black wrought iron metal staircase with polished timber stairs and ample space for understairs storage, built-in staircase lighting, door to hot press, door to bedroom one, games room, ground floor wc and open arch to living / dining / kitchen.\n\nLiving Dining Kitchen - 9.05m x 5.5m\nNote * Size does not include window spaceLiving Dining Area - Polished timber flooring, side aspect bay window with views of the Atlantic Ocean, recess ceiling lighting, raised solid fuel insert with polished flag and open access to kitchen area.Kitchen Area - Tile flooring, side aspect windows, recess ceiling lighting, built-in wall and base units with ample work surfaces, tile splash back, Belfast style double sink, wall mounted plate shelving, gas hob with double electric ovens underneath, space for large fridge freezer, pantry-style storage units, space for dishwasher, breakfast island with extended counter for breakfast seating and door to utility.\n\nUtility Room - 5.45m x 1.75m\nTiling flooring, rear door access, double Belfast-style sink, wall and base storage units, space and plumbing for washing machine and dryer, this area also houses the oil burner.\n\nGames Room - 5.5m x 3.8m\nSolid timber and front and side aspect windows.\n\nBedroom One - 5.45m x 3.95m\nTimber flooring, dual aspect windows to front and rear, recess ceiling lighting, built-in fan and door to ground floor wc.\n\nGround Floor Shower Room - 3.4m x 2m\nFully tiled from ceiling to floor, rear aspect window, low-level wc, wash hand basin with overhead fitted mirror and electric light, corner fitted walk-in pump shower area with decorative glass screens and heated towel rail.\n\nFirst Floor Landing - 4.8m x 7.4m\nArchitecturally designed gable-end ceiling-to-floor four-panel windows with fantastic views over the Atlantic Ocean and the Aran Islands, velux window, polished timber flooring, raised stove and doors to bedrooms two, three and four and shower room.\n\nBedroom Two - 5.2m x 3.85m\nTimber flooring, rear aspect window and velux window to the side, offering fantastic views, polished timber flooring and built-in lighting.\n\nBedroom Three - 4.7m x 3.85m\nLarge double room with window to the front and a velux window to the side, polished timber flooring and decorative light fitting.\n\nShower Room - 1.35m x 3.4m\nFully tiled ceiling to floor, corner pump shower unit, quality hand basin with overhead fitted mirror and electric light, and low-level WC.\n\nBedroom Four - 4.2m x 3.85m\nPolished timber flooring, double velux windows and outstanding views, feature wallpapered walls on all sides, decorative light fitting and built-in fan.\n\nEn-Suite - 3.8m x 1.8m\nFully tiled ceiling to floor, low-level wc, quality hand basin with overhead built-in mirror and light, corner bath unit and overhead corner shower nozzle,\n\nDetached Storage Shed - 3.65m x 2.75m\nConcrete floor.\n\nOutside - \nFront - Set on approximately one acre, the property has a paddock area with road frontage to the front of the site, which may offer further potential. It also has a grass area to the side and a pea gravel meandering driveway.Rear - Large patio extending the full lenght of the rear of the property with cut stone walls leading onto the lawn area.\n\n"
      },
